text:
Mules, doctors, tailors, and lawyers,

running through the streets by the millions;

dukes, lackeys, ladies, and informers,

all bundled together without distinction;


a great rabble of tolerated petty hidalgos,

whose examination was made by doubloons,

and a patch of midwife devils

who feel the wave of married men;


a thousand tax-farmers by excellence;

mangy men turned into lords;

every vice under the name of decency;


it is a brothel of idlers and layabouts,

where there is supreme freedom of conscience

for idiots, slanderers, and swindlers.
